# Contract v1.3: the composition shows only in the panel's input line (pinyin with syllable spaces, a draft as
# "improve › ok"), never as marked text in the field; the field gets text only on commit.
NAME a Chromium field cleared during a pinyin composition has empty context
PROFILES chromium electron
LANG chinese
TEXT "old|"
TYPE nihao
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT preedit "ni hao"
APP clears
# Contract v1.3: nothing of "nihao" was in the field, so the app emptying it leaves it empty: no pinyin for the page to
# commit, nothing read before the caret. The input method may keep the composition in its panel (acceptable) or drop
# it; the user's next step either way is Esc, which leaves no composition, and then a fresh one with no "nihao" in it.
EXPECT doc ""
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT context before ""
KEY esc
EXPECT doc ""
EXPECT preedit none
TYPE wo
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT preedit "wo"
KEY space
EXPECT doc "我|"
EXPECT marked none
EXPECT preedit none
EXPECT panel hidden
EXPECT nolost
